.env*
# .env.example is committed to this public repo and holds no secrets, only key
# names. Next's output file tracing pulls it into the prebuilt function bundle,
# so excluding it from upload made every `vercel deploy --prebuilt` fail with
#     Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, readlink '/vercel/path0/.env.example'
# Un-ignoring it costs nothing and unblocks the deploy.
!.env.example
.next/
coverage/
node_modules/
playwright-report/
test-results/
